~ start
Beachgoer: Hey... glad you made it out here. Beach days sound relaxing in theory, right? Sun, waves, good vibes.
Beachgoer: But let me ask you something real quick— Have you ever stepped onto a beach and suddenly felt way more aware of your body than usual?
- Yeah... instantly.
    => beach_spotlight
- Sometimes, depends on the day.
    => beach_spotlight
- Not really.
    => beach_spotlight
- I try not to think about it.
    => beach_spotlight

~ beach_spotlight
Beachgoer: Yeah. Same. It's like the second you hit the sand, your brain flips on this spotlight you didn't ask for.
Beachgoer: You start noticing everything—your body, other people's bodies, what you're wearing, what you wish you looked like.
Beachgoer: And somehow it feels like everyone else is more confident, more comfortable, more... put together.
Beachgoer: But here's something important that doesn't get said enough— Most of the people you see out here? They're in their own heads too. They're adjusting, comparing, overthinking. Just like you.
Beachgoer: Let me ask you—when you look around and see someone you think looks "perfect"... what happens in your mind?
- I compare myself immediately.
    => comparison_mode
- I feel kind of insecure.
    => comparison_mode
- I try not to, but it still happens.
    => comparison_mode
- I remind myself it doesn't matter.
    => comparison_mode

~ comparison_mode
Beachgoer: All of those are super common. Your brain is wired to compare—it's trying to make sense of where you fit in.
Beachgoer: But at the beach, that instinct goes into overdrive. It's like comparison mode gets cranked to max volume.
Beachgoer: Just remember to give yourself some grace today. You deserve to enjoy the sun just as much as anyone else here.
Beachgoer: Ready to find a spot to sit? Just tap the screen when you are.
=> END